1905-06 was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 18th season of competitive football. They competed as trophy holders in the [[Scottish First Division]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1900/celtic1906.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1905-06|website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref> which they successfully retained. It was the second time Celtic won two league titles in a row, their 6th league title overall, and their 10th major domestic title. This was their second league title in route to a then record six league titles in a row.

Celtic reached the third round of the [[Scottish Cup]], but lost 1-2 home to [[Heart of Midlothian F.C.|Hearts]].They also won the [[Glasgow Cup]] this season.

